        {
          "id": "SP_CERITELLOPSIS_PLICATULA",
          "name": "Ceritellopsis plicatula",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Ceritellopsis",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "The largest specimen is 5.3 mm high. The shell is slender with a high and acute spire. The whorls are high and have a distinctly oblique ramp accentuating the sutures. The ramp is demarcated from whorl face by an angulation. The whorls are ornamented with broad axial ribs, that are fading on the last preserved whorls. The transition from whorl face to base is evenly rounded. The base is smooth. The damaged aperture is oval, acute adapically, and has a siphonal canal.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:10829979",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "c57db551-0157-54f-9fc-07f7d97b136b54"
